🚽 Test case: round-22 review finding #1, the non-int-base exhibit --
🚽 the bug wasn't specific to `skibidi *`: ANY user-defined function
🚽 returning a pointer to a non-int base type (`chad *`, `yap *`,
🚽 `cap *`, `smol *`) fell into that base type's ordinary SCALAR case in
🚽 handle_function_call() (VAR_FLOAT here), reinterpreting the raw
🚽 address bit pattern as if it were a float value stored directly in
🚽 the return box. Confirmed via a temporary A/B test (git stash to the
🚽 pre-fix commit) that this crashed with an ASan SEGV inside
🚽 evaluate_expression_float() reading through the mis-typed box.
chad *pass_float_ptr(chad *p) {
    bussin p;
}

skibidi main {
    chad y = 3.5;
    chad *q = pass_float_ptr(&y);
    yappin("%.1f\n", *q);
    bussin 0;
}
